<title>USA: Kansas fed cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas fed cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales of slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry good, demand moderate. Week-to-date 19,200 head confirmed including 15,500 head or about 81 percent of previously contracted or formulated cattle.</p>
<p>Last sale Tuesday at $64.00 per cwt, bids $64.00, asking prices $65.00-$66.00. Sales FOB feedlot net weights after 4 percent shrink. Confirmed - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
